<Prose title="Privacy" description="What Nerdy Birdie Gaming stores and what it doesn't.">
  <p class="muted">Last updated 24 November 2026.</p>
  <h2>The short version</h2>
  <p>No accounts, no analytics, no ads, no tracking cookies. Your progress stays in your browser.</p>
  <h2>What's stored on your device</h2>
  <p>When you tick an objective, save one or write a note, it's stored in your browser's local storage on this device, along with your
  spoiler and platform settings. It isn't sent to us. Clearing your browser's site data deletes it, so use
  <a href="/progress/">My progress</a> to download a backup.</p>
  <h2>What we don't collect</h2>
  <p>We don't run analytics or advertising scripts. Fonts are served from this site, not from a third party. If we ever add privacy-friendly
  usage stats, this page will say so first.</p>
  <h2>Hosting</h2>
  <p>Like any website, our hosting provider handles basic request logs (such as IP addresses) to deliver and protect the site.</p>
  <h2>Links to other sites</h2>
  <p>Links to Discord, cozmc.us, Rockstar Games and other sites open those sites, which have their own privacy policies. Videos will only load
  from YouTube after you choose to play them.</p>
</Prose>
